id: pm-apjlc4
title: Investigate native GitHub check waits that remain active after terminal checks
description: "Observed during PR1515: the native gh2.102.0 check watcher remained alive after a fresh head snapshot showed39successful checks and3skips. Its process was25minutes old. Interrupting only the read-only watcher and starting the reviews phase returned immediately with the accurate unresolved-conversation blocker. No CI job or required status was bypassed. Upstream cause and controlled reproduction remain unconfirmed."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,github,review
created_at: "2026-10-20T06:14:19.977Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T05:44:30.157Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce or explicitly attribute the stalled native watcher using terminal and genuinely pending controls; define bounded liveness behavior without certifying readiness from timeout or unavailable data; retain exact-head required publisher and conversation evidence; preserve the completed predecessor scope and record any upstream CLI issue.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: A stuck transport wait is distinguishable from pending hosted work and never becomes a false successful review receipt.
